            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for energetic, then the Persian for to be lazy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پیانو",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پیانو (piyâno) — \"a piano\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دخترم از هفت سالگی پیانو میزند. dokhtaram az haft sâlegi piyâno mizanad. My daughter has played the piano since she was seven."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian strikes an instrument: piyâno zadan 'to play the piano'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "piyâno is a modern loan, usually traced to French or Italian piano. EtymDB has no entry for the Persian word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
